      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $A∨(B∧¬C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:\n\n$$\nA∨(B∧¬C)≡(A∨B)∧(A∨¬C)\n$$\n\nNow, since $A∨B≡B∨A,$ we can write\n\n$$\n(A∨B)∧(A∨¬C)≡(B∨A)∧(A∨¬C).\n$$",
